<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ehsan Khan Kangarlu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ehsan Khan Nakhchivanski</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ehsan Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangarlu">Kangarlu</a> was a member of the Kangarlu dynasty of the Nakhichevan Khanate and the last of its khans. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1826-1828">Russo-Persian War</a> of 1826–1828 he went over to the Russians and surrendered the fortress of Abbasabad, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay">Treaty of Turkmenchay</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhichevan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> he served as its governor and a Russian officer.</p></div>
